  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in South Dakota totaled $566M in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 3,004 awards with an average award size of $188K. Obligations are down 29.6% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations have varied: FY21 recorded $624M, FY22 recorded $1.2B, FY23 recorded $1B, FY24 recorded $1.3B, and FY25 recorded $804M. The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency with $246M in obligations, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $110M and the Department of the Interior with $94M. KBR WYLE SERVICES, LLC is the largest vendor with $68.3M in obligations. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry by obligations with $134M, and Computer Facilities Management Services follows with $68.6M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did FY2026 obligations compare with prior years?",
        "body": "FY2026 obligations stand at $566M. FY25 obligations were $804M and FY24 obligations were $1.3B. Obligations are down 29.6% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers, vendors, and industries in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer with $246M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $110M and the Department of the Interior with $94M. KBR WYLE SERVICES, LLC leads vendors with $68.3M, followed by CONTI FEDERAL SERVICES, LLC with $42.3M and FEDERAL CONTRACTING INC with $40.6M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction leads industries with $134M, followed by Computer Facilities Management Services with $68.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
